WEBVTT

00:00:18.010 --> 00:00:23.750
<i>Every day I keep wondering if</i>
<i>there's something missing.</i>

00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:31.090
<i>I still want to keep feeling my</i>
<i>heart beating in anticipation.</i>

00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:38.830
<i>Ideals are far out of reach, but</i>
<i>reality is within my grasp.</i>

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:44.900
<i>It's not easy standing against the wind,</i>
<i>but as long as I keep smiling...</i>

00:00:45.010 --> 00:00:49.680
<i>... staying true to myself,</i>
<i>I'll become stronger.</i>

00:00:49.880 --> 00:00:57.450
<i>I know I'll love somebody. Someday</i>
<i>I'll find him and take my chance.</i>

00:00:57.520 --> 00:01:04.430
<i>I'll make the whole world stop</i>
<i>to see the angel that I'll be.</i>

00:01:04.490 --> 00:01:12.360
<i>I know I'll love somebody. Someday</i>
<i>I'll meet the man of my dreams.</i>

00:01:12.470 --> 00:01:20.030
<i>Nothing can slow me down. Tomorrow</i>
<i>is just around the corner.</i>

00:01:35.620 --> 00:01:36.820
There's no doubt
about it.

00:01:36.930 --> 00:01:38.690
It's the work of the
same thieves.

00:01:38.790 --> 00:01:41.520
This is where they loaded
the stolen cars.

00:01:41.700 --> 00:01:44.530
Unbelievable. Right under
Headquarters' nose.

00:01:44.970 --> 00:01:48.400
Just as we strengthened our
patrols at the port facilities.

00:01:48.570 --> 00:01:53.030
By using a boat, they're able
to make offshore deliveries.

00:01:53.310 --> 00:01:54.410
I see.

00:01:54.410 --> 00:01:55.840
See what?

00:01:56.010 --> 00:02:00.950
Call in the Maritime Safety Agency
and the Harbor Police.

00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:02.520
Yes.

00:02:02.520 --> 00:02:03.110
Tsujimoto.

00:02:03.290 --> 00:02:08.220
I'll get each station to step up
their patrol of the waterways.

00:02:10.860 --> 00:02:12.990
Excuse me.

00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:16.120
<i>Miyuki.</i>

00:02:18.530 --> 00:02:21.000
Come in, Headquarters.
This is Unit 3.

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:26.110
FILE. 50
THE INVESTIGATION
AT BOKUTO STATION

00:02:31.380 --> 00:02:32.880
Where's Miyuki?

00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:34.180
In the garage.

00:02:34.350 --> 00:02:38.080
Working on her patrol car again?
That's all she ever does lately.

00:02:38.820 --> 00:02:41.080
I guess there's
a hole.

00:02:41.620 --> 00:02:43.590
A hole? In the car?

00:02:43.590 --> 00:02:45.790
I'm talking about Natsumi.

00:02:45.890 --> 00:02:50.630
Miyuki's trying desperately to fill
the void that Natsumi left.

00:02:50.730 --> 00:02:54.070
That's why she is slaving
over the car.

00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:58.960
Hmm. The Natsumi
void, huh?

00:02:59.140 --> 00:03:02.340
Ladies? Can I offer
you some rice?

00:03:03.040 --> 00:03:04.670
Why do you
ask?

00:03:04.850 --> 00:03:09.610
I forgot that Natsumi's not around, and
made the usual amount of rice.

00:03:11.550 --> 00:03:14.820
I guess the void she
left is pretty big.

00:03:14.990 --> 00:03:16.790
I'd love some.

00:03:22.500 --> 00:03:25.490
Aoi! This is
delicious!

00:03:27.800 --> 00:03:30.200
You should eat
a proper lunch.

00:03:30.370 --> 00:03:33.140
I like eating outside
like this.

00:03:33.310 --> 00:03:36.280
You have to look after
yourself, you know.

00:03:36.440 --> 00:03:39.740
It all has to do with what's
in these rice balls.

00:03:39.920 --> 00:03:41.380
Are you even listening
to me?

00:03:41.550 --> 00:03:45.610
I can't sit back and relax with those
thieves still sneaking around.

00:03:50.960 --> 00:03:53.620
I guess you're worried
about Natsumi, huh?

00:03:55.330 --> 00:03:58.320
So much for
lunch.

00:03:58.500 --> 00:03:59.990
Hey!

00:04:00.170 --> 00:04:02.030
Let's get back
to work!

00:04:02.200 --> 00:04:03.970
Yum.

00:04:05.010 --> 00:04:06.310
Aah!

00:04:06.310 --> 00:04:07.340
What?

00:04:07.340 --> 00:04:08.810
Our lips touched the same place!

00:04:08.810 --> 00:04:10.780
Don't be silly!

00:04:11.280 --> 00:04:13.840
Miyuki.

00:04:23.630 --> 00:04:25.620
That must
be them.

00:04:26.630 --> 00:04:30.360
Do a plate search for me.
Shinagawa plate, #35...

00:04:32.170 --> 00:04:33.830
They noticed us!

00:04:48.850 --> 00:04:52.550
We have no registration
for that plate.

00:04:53.620 --> 00:04:56.250
So it's a
fake.

00:05:01.160 --> 00:05:04.130
You, in the Mercedes!
Pull over!

00:05:15.980 --> 00:05:17.910
Nakajima!

00:05:20.920 --> 00:05:23.040
I'll never forgive
you!

00:05:39.800 --> 00:05:40.860
Miyuki!

00:05:41.040 --> 00:05:42.940
We're fine! We can
go even faster.

00:05:43.040 --> 00:05:47.000
I've been tuning it up! That's what
the triple nitro tanks were for!

00:05:48.310 --> 00:05:50.170
<i>I'll catch him</i>
<i>for sure!</i>

00:05:50.280 --> 00:05:56.420
<i>I will!</i>

00:06:24.710 --> 00:06:27.080
My car...

00:06:34.660 --> 00:06:36.360
Ow! Ow!

00:06:36.360 --> 00:06:38.330
Pipe down. You're a man, aren't you?

00:06:38.490 --> 00:06:39.490
Owww...

00:06:39.490 --> 00:06:42.430
You're lucky you got off so easy.

00:06:42.430 --> 00:06:44.770
But, Chief!

00:06:44.770 --> 00:06:49.470
Didn't you carry a gun as well?

00:06:49.700 --> 00:06:52.970
There's someone who's been
hurt more seriously.

00:06:58.110 --> 00:07:01.610
I'm so sorry, car.

00:07:05.850 --> 00:07:07.050
"Meeting Room"

00:07:07.420 --> 00:07:11.920
We cannot have these thieves
prowling around with guns!

00:07:12.590 --> 00:07:17.900
Starting at noon, we'll do complete
sweeps from south to north.

00:07:18.430 --> 00:07:20.560
From now on, we're working
around-the-clock!

00:07:20.740 --> 00:07:22.700
Sir!

00:07:24.440 --> 00:07:25.470
Kobayakawa.

00:07:25.470 --> 00:07:26.530
Yes?

00:07:26.710 --> 00:07:29.540
I want you to stay and
coordinate.

00:07:30.710 --> 00:07:32.680
Yes.

00:07:47.400 --> 00:07:51.020
Yotsugi. Shin Yotsugi. Kinegawa
Bridge. Dispatch complete.

00:07:51.130 --> 00:07:54.000
Ryoogoku Bridge, Kototoi Bridge
traffic lane control.

00:07:54.500 --> 00:07:57.160
Unit B, head for Kuramae
Bridge.

00:07:57.340 --> 00:08:00.710
Roger. Kobayakawa, are
you staying there?

00:08:00.880 --> 00:08:02.210
Nakajima?

00:08:02.210 --> 00:08:04.370
I'm counting on your instructions.

00:08:04.550 --> 00:08:06.740
No personal conver-
sations here.

00:08:06.920 --> 00:08:08.640
So, what are you
going to do?

00:08:08.820 --> 00:08:09.350
Huh?

00:08:09.350 --> 00:08:11.510
About the car. Aren't you going to fix it?

00:08:11.690 --> 00:08:14.480
What are you saying?
We're on duty.

00:08:16.620 --> 00:08:18.090
"Shiba-Ken Delivery"

00:08:18.090 --> 00:08:22.620
Sorry, something's wrong with
my radio. What'd you say?
"Shiba-Ken Delivery"

00:08:22.800 --> 00:08:25.060
I said we're
on duty!

00:08:25.170 --> 00:08:27.260
Anyway...

00:08:27.440 --> 00:08:29.270
Yes?

00:08:29.270 --> 00:08:31.240
I can't fix it.

00:08:31.410 --> 00:08:32.970
What?

00:08:32.970 --> 00:08:35.030
That's not true.

00:08:35.140 --> 00:08:37.750
You can get all the parts. And I'm sure...

00:08:37.750 --> 00:08:42.010
I can't fix absolutely everything, you know.

00:08:42.420 --> 00:08:44.350
Natsumi and I built
that car.

00:08:44.450 --> 00:08:47.980
We did it together.

00:08:48.920 --> 00:08:50.980
Kobayakawa.

00:08:51.230 --> 00:08:55.990
That car was like
a part of us.

00:08:56.430 --> 00:08:59.490
But look what
I did to it.

00:09:00.270 --> 00:09:03.240
The car was crying out, but
I didn't even notice.

00:09:06.610 --> 00:09:09.200
I'm a failure as
a mechanic.

00:09:09.310 --> 00:09:12.510
I can't possibly face
Natsumi now.

00:09:12.610 --> 00:09:15.520
Maybe I should
just quit.

00:09:15.820 --> 00:09:17.050
Huh?

00:09:17.050 --> 00:09:19.380
What are you going to do after you quit?

00:09:19.890 --> 00:09:22.650
What would you do if
you weren't a cop?

00:09:22.760 --> 00:09:25.390
Is there something else you
think you'd be better at?

00:09:25.490 --> 00:09:29.620
Is there anything that could replace
that car, in your heart?!

00:09:30.270 --> 00:09:31.900
Nakajima.

00:09:31.900 --> 00:09:36.130
I can't take its place.

00:09:39.410 --> 00:09:42.140
Over and out.

00:09:51.790 --> 00:09:52.850
Chief!

00:09:52.850 --> 00:09:56.020
You shouldn't be talking
about personal matters.

00:09:56.190 --> 00:09:57.860
I'm sorry.

00:09:57.860 --> 00:10:03.360
I'm sorry.
Tell Nakajima I want to see him, too.

00:10:03.360 --> 00:10:03.500
Tell Nakajima I want to see him, too.

00:10:03.500 --> 00:10:05.470
Yes.

00:10:25.520 --> 00:10:29.250
Hi! This is Miyuki and Natsumi's place.
We can't come to the phone...

00:10:29.360 --> 00:10:32.820
...but make sure to leave your
name and a message.

00:10:32.990 --> 00:10:33.360
<i>Guess I should change the message.</i>

00:10:33.360 --> 00:10:37.730
No hanging up on us!

00:10:48.110 --> 00:10:50.300
"Used Car Sales"

00:11:01.690 --> 00:11:03.660
"You win!"

00:11:05.490 --> 00:11:07.550
Hmph.

00:11:08.230 --> 00:11:11.430
Unit 7 didn't report seeing any suspicious-
looking cars in the south.

00:11:11.600 --> 00:11:14.070
Same in the north.

00:11:14.470 --> 00:11:16.340
So there are no leads.

00:11:16.340 --> 00:11:18.400
That's not true.

00:11:20.740 --> 00:11:22.210
The used car lots?

00:11:22.210 --> 00:11:26.480
The used car lots?
Scrap yards bought the cars cheaply...

00:11:26.950 --> 00:11:28.850
...but there are
no records.

00:11:29.250 --> 00:11:30.590
They're the thieves?

00:11:30.590 --> 00:11:34.490
We'll know soon. Where's Nakajima?

00:11:34.590 --> 00:11:38.360
I've got to show him a thing
or two about being a man.

00:11:38.560 --> 00:11:42.860
Were you listening in?
How about that...

00:11:48.700 --> 00:11:50.300
It's a three
hour wait.

00:11:50.470 --> 00:11:52.770
I'll wait.

00:11:52.940 --> 00:11:54.910
H... H... Hey, wait
a second!

00:11:55.310 --> 00:11:57.540
Don't think you can
get away with this.

00:11:57.710 --> 00:11:59.940
How could you treat
Miyuki that way?

00:12:00.110 --> 00:12:01.250
Well, uh...

00:12:01.250 --> 00:12:02.650
Not good enough!

00:12:02.750 --> 00:12:09.120
Only you can
cheer her up.

00:12:09.520 --> 00:12:13.020
All you had to do was say
something sweet to her.

00:12:13.190 --> 00:12:15.490
Yes, I know,
but...

00:12:15.660 --> 00:12:20.170
It's that wishy-washy attitude of
yours that's the problem.

00:12:21.340 --> 00:12:23.200
So, have you
been busy?

00:12:23.370 --> 00:12:24.510
Yes.

00:12:24.510 --> 00:12:26.060
How's the patrol car running?

00:12:26.240 --> 00:12:29.840
I'm not driving it right now.
It's broken down.

00:12:30.010 --> 00:12:35.380
That's no good. Cars are like women.
They get lonely if you ignore them.

00:12:35.550 --> 00:12:39.010
Hey, why are you saying things
like that to Miyuki?

00:12:39.190 --> 00:12:40.880
Oh, uh...

00:12:40.990 --> 00:12:44.050
I didn't mean it like that,
I just meant... uh...

00:12:44.230 --> 00:12:45.890
It's no good.

00:12:45.990 --> 00:12:48.520
It's like I couldn't get
enough parts.

00:12:49.230 --> 00:12:52.530
Somehow it just seems
like there's a big hole.

00:12:52.830 --> 00:12:55.960
It's not that
old.

00:12:56.070 --> 00:12:58.130
I'll help you find
the parts.

00:12:58.310 --> 00:13:00.140
No, that's not
what I meant.

00:13:00.310 --> 00:13:03.000
I wouldn't want to take
that away from you.

00:13:03.110 --> 00:13:08.010
Searching for the parts
is half the fun, isn't it?

00:13:24.430 --> 00:13:27.490
Searching is half
the fun, huh?

00:13:27.670 --> 00:13:29.570
Miyuki!

00:13:31.570 --> 00:13:33.870
There's been another
theft!

00:13:34.040 --> 00:13:35.310
What?

00:13:35.310 --> 00:13:38.040
They stole a BMW.

00:13:38.210 --> 00:13:43.620
We got a call about a guy with a fork lift,
who was trying to lift the car away.

00:13:43.850 --> 00:13:44.850
Really?

00:13:44.850 --> 00:13:48.690
He looked strange and wore a mask.

00:13:48.860 --> 00:13:50.380
It wouldn't possibly
be...

00:13:53.560 --> 00:13:54.630
It's Strike Man!

00:13:54.630 --> 00:13:57.060
Hmm?

00:13:57.170 --> 00:14:00.400
Who calls my name with
such familiarity?!

00:14:00.670 --> 00:14:02.660
What do you think
you're doing?

00:14:02.840 --> 00:14:07.770
Just what it looks like! Punishing
an illegal parker!

00:14:07.880 --> 00:14:13.400
My new weapon, Super Tiger Zarathrustra Strike the
Third, will take this auto to where it belongs.

00:14:16.420 --> 00:14:19.650
How can he be doing this to
us at such a crucial time?!

00:14:20.820 --> 00:14:25.160
Aren't you the sidekick of my arch-
enemy, Home Run Girl?

00:14:25.460 --> 00:14:27.090
Sidekick?!

00:14:27.090 --> 00:14:29.860
Miyuki. Don't let him get to you.

00:14:30.030 --> 00:14:33.660
I won't speak with you! Bring
out Home Run Girl!

00:14:33.900 --> 00:14:37.630
Natsumi's not here! I'm the one
who's going to catch you!

00:14:38.310 --> 00:14:44.140
What? You're going to face me with those
weak arms of yours? Let's see you try!

00:14:47.220 --> 00:14:50.180
You mean, this is
the challenge?

00:14:51.390 --> 00:14:52.880
Get a load
of this!

00:14:52.990 --> 00:14:54.920
Try and hit my
Devil Ball...

00:14:55.020 --> 00:14:59.290
...the Tornado
Fork Lift...

00:14:59.390 --> 00:15:00.830
...Crash!

00:15:10.040 --> 00:15:13.010
Great hit, Miyuki!

00:15:13.010 --> 00:15:14.630
Great hit, Miyuki!
Hey! I hit it!

00:15:14.810 --> 00:15:20.650
How dare she dismiss the pitch that
I've worked so hard to develop?!

00:15:21.650 --> 00:15:25.610
Who would have thought I'd go down in
defeat to a thin little woman like her?!

00:15:25.850 --> 00:15:27.550
Excuse me.

00:15:27.720 --> 00:15:33.680
You haven't seen the last of me. I will
knock you down the next time.

00:15:33.790 --> 00:15:35.760
Look forward
to it!

00:15:37.400 --> 00:15:40.090
Stop right
there!

00:15:40.270 --> 00:15:41.960
Well, well.

00:15:42.070 --> 00:15:44.090
I can do it!

00:15:51.910 --> 00:15:55.870
This weighs a ton. I can't believe
she actually used these.

00:15:57.550 --> 00:15:59.520
All right!

00:16:05.260 --> 00:16:06.990
I don't believe this.

00:16:06.990 --> 00:16:08.700
Is it some kind of depressive fit?

00:16:08.700 --> 00:16:11.670
I hear she broke up with Nakajima.

00:16:11.830 --> 00:16:13.800
More rice,
please!

00:16:15.070 --> 00:16:17.040
Excuse me!

00:16:27.720 --> 00:16:29.680
Point!

00:16:45.400 --> 00:16:47.560
Ow.

00:16:59.410 --> 00:17:01.380
Nakajima.

00:17:03.680 --> 00:17:06.590
How come you're riding
a bike all of a sudden?

00:17:07.720 --> 00:17:08.960
Doesn't suit me?

00:17:08.960 --> 00:17:10.920
Doesn't suit me?
It's not bad.

00:17:13.130 --> 00:17:15.560
I've been
thinking.

00:17:15.660 --> 00:17:19.430
It's a lot more fun to try experimenting
with things...

00:17:19.530 --> 00:17:23.370
...as opposed to getting caught
up in your own little world.

00:17:24.110 --> 00:17:26.370
I'm still young,
too. Right?

00:17:28.840 --> 00:17:35.440
I'm going to try lots of things. At work,
and at the batting center. And also...

00:17:36.720 --> 00:17:39.350
Love.

00:17:43.720 --> 00:17:47.850
I'm going to try all kinds of things.
And search for my own parts.

00:17:48.260 --> 00:17:50.890
Maybe I was wrong
about this, though.

00:17:51.070 --> 00:17:54.130
I think you should go
for it. I'll teach you.

00:17:54.300 --> 00:17:55.370
Will you?

00:17:55.370 --> 00:17:57.740
Will you?
But I'm a tough coach, you know.

00:17:57.910 --> 00:18:01.310
A rough one, huh? That's
okay with me.

00:18:01.480 --> 00:18:03.710
You!

00:18:03.880 --> 00:18:05.280
She's okay.

00:18:05.280 --> 00:18:07.750
She's okay.
After the rain, the calm...

00:18:08.250 --> 00:18:09.920
What are you doing?

00:18:09.920 --> 00:18:11.980
What are you doing?
Social studies.

00:18:16.890 --> 00:18:18.650
The wind's
picked up.

00:18:18.830 --> 00:18:22.130
Oh. The wind's
picked up.

00:18:22.300 --> 00:18:24.060
"Bokuto Station"

00:18:24.670 --> 00:18:27.960
There have been three new luxury
car thefts recently.

00:18:28.900 --> 00:18:33.860
Judging by the locations, it is very likely
the thieves are still in the city.

00:18:34.640 --> 00:18:38.480
As such, we will mount extra patrols
to pursue these criminals.

00:18:39.050 --> 00:18:44.010
I will have Sgt. Kobayakawa, our coordinator,
explain the plan.

00:18:47.320 --> 00:18:50.480
This is our
strategy.

00:19:06.870 --> 00:19:09.240
Kobayakawa!

00:19:10.040 --> 00:19:11.580
Nakajima.

00:19:11.580 --> 00:19:13.440
Nakajima.
Let's do our best.

00:19:13.610 --> 00:19:16.580
Yeah.

00:19:16.750 --> 00:19:18.680
I don't understand
you, either.

00:19:19.090 --> 00:19:22.990
So after all that, you actually
are getting along all right.

00:19:23.360 --> 00:19:24.120
Huh?

00:19:24.120 --> 00:19:29.790
Maybe he's going to ask you
out after this case is over.

00:19:29.960 --> 00:19:31.130
No, it's nothing like that.

00:19:31.130 --> 00:19:32.000
Come on.

00:19:32.000 --> 00:19:37.100
He said he couldn't take the place of my car.

00:19:37.100 --> 00:19:39.900
Do you really believe that?

00:19:40.070 --> 00:19:41.580
What do you mean?

00:19:41.580 --> 00:19:44.100
What do you mean?
He can't express his feelings, that's all.

00:19:44.210 --> 00:19:47.770
The other day, I was going to
tell him to forget about you.

00:19:47.880 --> 00:19:50.650
You know what
he said?

00:19:52.650 --> 00:19:56.610
<i>"Sure I could try</i>
<i>to comfort her."</i>

00:19:57.220 --> 00:19:59.420
<i>"But that wouldn't</i>
<i>be for the best."</i>

00:19:59.530 --> 00:20:04.490
<i>"I'd rather be there for her once she's</i>
<i>worked this out for herself."</i>

00:20:05.430 --> 00:20:11.340
Nakajima cares about you
more than anyone.

00:20:12.310 --> 00:20:14.300
Miyuki?

00:20:18.780 --> 00:20:21.210
What's the
matter?

00:20:21.380 --> 00:20:23.710
You're really pushy
sometimes.

00:20:23.880 --> 00:20:26.850
What's with all
this gloom?

00:20:30.290 --> 00:20:31.890
Natsumi!

00:20:31.890 --> 00:20:35.790
Get into your position, Miss Strategist.

00:20:44.570 --> 00:20:46.970
So it's all
fixed up.

00:20:47.070 --> 00:20:48.970
I heard all the
rumors.

00:20:49.140 --> 00:20:52.110
I'm still looking
for some parts.

00:20:52.280 --> 00:20:54.710
Wow. Sure it
won't break?

00:20:54.880 --> 00:20:55.780
You're right.

00:20:55.880 --> 00:20:59.010
We might go over the weight
capacity if you get in.

00:20:59.190 --> 00:21:00.890
Thanks a lot.

00:21:00.890 --> 00:21:02.380
Thanks a lot.
Just kidding.

00:21:02.560 --> 00:21:06.050
I didn't come here just to
hear about some parts.

00:21:06.630 --> 00:21:10.060
It's a big mistake to think we can
just carry on like before.

00:21:10.970 --> 00:21:12.930
For both of us.
For both of us.

00:21:21.540 --> 00:21:26.500
Let's do our best, huh. This is the
beginning of a new future for us.

00:21:56.280 --> 00:22:02.480
<i>Every time I fall</i>
<i>out of love...</i>

00:22:02.550 --> 00:22:12.390
<i>... everything that I see</i>
<i>turns monochrome.</i>

00:22:12.990 --> 00:22:19.290
<i>We often used to go see the</i>
<i>games at the stadium...</i>

00:22:19.400 --> 00:22:29.410
<i>... but the good old days mean</i>
<i>nothing to me anymore.</i>

00:22:29.480 --> 00:22:43.320
<i>Even after you've gone, I still wanna</i>
<i>tell the world what it is that I love.</i>

00:22:43.660 --> 00:22:51.600
<i>Looking up to the sky, I try</i>
<i>holding back the tears.</i>

00:22:51.670 --> 00:23:00.240
<i>Flags were moving in the wind and</i>
<i>things seemed brighter yesterday.</i>

00:23:00.470 --> 00:23:08.320
<i>Looking up to the sky, we used</i>
<i>to talk about our dreams.</i>

00:23:08.380 --> 00:23:17.890
<i>No matter how far out of reach they seemed,</i>
<i>dreams could come true, or so it felt.</i>

00:23:18.260 --> 00:23:25.330
<i>Tell me that that fire in your</i>
<i>eyes was not a lie.</i>

00:23:29.800 --> 00:23:31.400
Bokuto...

00:23:31.570 --> 00:23:33.600
...which means East
of Sumida River...

00:23:33.770 --> 00:23:35.610
It's a wonderful town.

00:23:36.340 --> 00:23:40.140
When in the area, please
drop by Bokuto Station.

00:23:40.410 --> 00:23:42.010
We will make you feel
very welcome.

00:23:43.620 --> 00:23:47.250
Next time, You're Under
Arrest, File 51...

00:23:47.420 --> 00:23:49.920
...Bokuto's Best Investigation Partners.

00:23:49.920 --> 00:23:51.930
You're Under Arrest!
